  "grafo_evidencia": {
    "nodes": [
      {
        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "c7bbc6a5-a33b-5056-9694-1d0326c65a12",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: German Spitz, Keeshond, Norfolk Spaniel, English Springer Spaniel, Sussex Spaniel, Clumber Spaniel\n- Concepts: dog breeds, breed categories, springer-type spaniels, breed naming, breed registration\n\nFacts:\n- German Spitz is used to refer both to a specific breed of dog and to a broader category or type of dog.\n- Several modern dog breeds were developed from the German Spitz and are registered either as separate breeds or as varieties of German Spitz.\n- The term Norfolk Spaniel was used for springer-type spaniels that were neither Sussex Spaniels nor Clumber Spaniels.\n- Attempts were made to use Norfolk Spaniel to specify a breed that later became known as the English Springer Spaniel.\n- Keeshond was originally called the German Spitz, more specifically the Wolfspitz.\n- In 1926 in England, the name of the dog breed known as the German Spitz or Wolfspitz was officially changed to Keeshond.\n- In England, the Keeshond had been known as the Dutch Barge Dog before its official renaming in 1926.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "62d2ad5e-973d-5cf0-84fe-df6ae40bafc5",
        "text": "Page: German Spitz. Sentence: German Spitz is used to refer to both a breed of dog and category or type of dog.\nPage: German Spitz. Sentence: Several modern breeds have been developed from the German Spitz, and are either registered as separate breeds or as varieties of German Spitz.\nPage: Norfolk Spaniel. Sentence: The term was used to designate springer type spaniels that were neither Sussex nor Clumber Spaniels, and attempts were made to use it to specify a breed that would later become known as the English Springer Spaniel.\nPage: Keeshond. Sentence: Originally called the German Spitz, more specifically the Wolfspitz, the name was officially changed to Keeshond, in 1926 in England, where it had been known as the Dutch Barge Dog.",
